      "criterion": "Outside `mode: pre`, after planning but before any write, `version` refuses with E121 when a canonical manifest's on-disk effective version differs from its version at `HEAD`, or when its effective version staged in the git index differs from `HEAD`, provided a changeset remains in the `HEAD` tree or configured working-tree changesets directory (including untracked files), or a canonical manifest is staged. Staged metadata-only edits with unchanged effective versions are allowed. During `mode: exit`, already-written prerelease versions may be finalized to stable versions; a changed stable version is not exempt and is refused on retry. This detects interrupted applies without consuming retained inputs or stacking a second bump. A repository with no commits yet, a manifest/changesets directory that didn't exist at `HEAD`, or an active `mode: pre` cycle (which legitimately reruns `version` without a commit in between) is not refused this way.",
      "is_error_case": true
